WEBVTT

00:26:58.186 --> 00:27:01.717
from including their recommendations
as one input into our decisions.

00:27:03.687 --> 00:27:05.783
But there's still one missing piece.

00:27:05.807 --> 00:27:08.917
A piece that I learned to appreciate
through trial and error.

00:27:08.941 --> 00:27:10.138
Mostly error.

00:27:10.162 --> 00:27:11.352
CM: You're human, Adam.

00:27:11.376 --> 00:27:12.535
You're a human, Adam.

00:27:12.559 --> 00:27:13.717
AG: Damn it.

00:27:13.741 --> 00:27:15.638
Remember that guy I didn't want to hire

00:27:15.662 --> 00:27:17.701
because he didn't make enough eye contact?

00:27:17.725 --> 00:27:19.996
A colleague convinced me
to try another approach

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.962
with him and the other candidates.

00:27:21.986 --> 00:27:25.473
Since it was a sales job,
we gave candidates a sales task.

00:27:25.497 --> 00:27:28.543
We challenged them
to sell us a rotten apple.

00:27:29.003 --> 00:27:30.982
The no-eye-contact guy said,